; Sprites: spinning slab (4 frames), crawler (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $AB00+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like a flat box with a label window turning (front,
; oblique, edge-on, oblique); frames 4-7 look like a bug with antennae and legs scuttling. Used by entity definitions
; $65 $66 in rooms $1B $1E $24.
@label=SpritesSlabCrawler
b$AB00 DEFB $00,$00 ; frame 0: slab, front view (box with window, dotted base)
